  "worked_solution": "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=5i+3j,\\,a=-i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $3$ seconds, the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(5i+3j)+(-i+2j)(3) \\\\  & =(5i+3j)+(-3i+6j) \\\\  & =(2i+9j)\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|2i+9j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+81} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{85} \\\\  & \u22489.22\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places.",
